hoever  picks you you don't know if you're gonna  go first you don't know if you're gonna  last for us to get picked as a dream  come true and then all of a sudden you  feel like you're not accepted into this  organization or you already have this  added pressure because where you got  selected and and that that's not really  fair to the kid but at the same time  they  it's you learned that that's what comes  with the profession of playing  professional football at this level just  having to handle the fan bases handle  having to handle the the the situation  and pressure of the position you're in  now and it's just all part of the  learning process so I think at the same  time it puts a chip on your shoulder I  know it did for me everybody who doubted  me and thought I didn't deserve to be  picked number two overall I think I'm  still trying to prove those people wrong  to this day and that's something Daniel  is gonna have to do but at the same time  we're living the dream it's a dream come  true we're very blessed to be in the  situation and it really doesn't matter  if you get picked first second or get  picked in the sixth or seventh round  it's it's an amazing opportunity to play  at this level and all it all comes down  to what you make out of this opportunity  now so that's what what I've been trying  to do but you know if he calls you up  and he says you know Mitch they set  aside the whole UNC Duke thing how help  me out here give me something specific  give me something that I can do to get  through these early stages of all this  criticism all this pressure how am I  supposed to turn this into a positive  yeah definitely number one I would say  you got to block out everybody on the  outside you got to block out the media  Twitter everybody who's hating on your  situation and and trying to say that you  don't deserve it and then when you get  to the facility it's all about football  and I kind of know Daniel because I have  a good friend that coaches that