nd we're just way more focused on what  we want this offense to be how can we  can prove how we can be more explosive  convert more third downs score more  points and everything like that so just  it's made this transition going into  year three so much easier going into  year two of this offense just knowing  everyone who we have on playmaker wise  knowing your teammates all across the  board we didn't add a bunch of new guys  besides the rookies we just drafted so  we'll get that man and and we just have  great chemistry between the players on  offense and our coaches and what we're  trying to do scheme wise and we're just  so much further from where we're at so  I'm very excited to wear this offense  can be this year all right so phenomenal  year last year we all know how it ended  we don't have to go back through there I  will mention that week 17 the Vikings  rolled over I still can't believe that  but it ended poorly the Bears are  bringing in  eight kickers to try out we threw out  the idea today how far of a field goal  what's your longest field goal and do  you think you could kick a field goal in  the NFL in the game if you need to be  not saying you're gonna be say there's  an injury yeah yeah I heard I might get  thrown into the competition as well so I  kind of been working on my leg just in  case and you never know if it came down  to it I think I can make a 35 40 yarder  with the window I'm not gonna lie to you  I need the wind I need that strong  Chicago wind right at my back and I  think I got 35 in me maybe 40 if I get a  good little win behind me  old-school straight on straight on you  know in the old days that that would be  the biggest decision he'd probably be  spur the moment I used to toe kick  because youthful fall we would be the  only team the kick field goals and I'll  kick the field goals and then you start  to learn a soccer style to get more  power but if it came down to it I might  have to toe toe punch it you know get it  up there and see if we could get it  through you know one of the things that  the media types do before a game they're  always watching the kicker what's his  range how far is he making it does the  wind affect him do you pay any attention  to what your kicker looks like before a  game just so you know you know that  third and four from the 30 it's gonna be  more important than otherwise would be  because I'll have a whole lot of faith  in my guy today I actually I actually  don't I never paid attention to that  it's a couple times it's not our kicker  I pay attention to it's the other guy  because the the opposing teams kicker is  usually in our way when we're trying to  throw and we're like all right is this  guy done kicking yet we're trying to get  our warm-up in I'm trying to throw  routes and we're kept we're trying to go  around um and you try to be courteous or  whatever and not getting each other's  way because everyone's just got to get  to warm up in but I was you just  standing behind the opposing teams  kicker and you're like when's this guy  can move hey Vic Fangio is gone now he's  the defense coordinator last year did a  great job for the team whatwhat's that  transition going to be like I know  that's not your side of the ball but  it's gonna be seeing a lot of that side  of the ball in practice  yeah for sure we got a super talented  defense and  I know they're excited for Coach Pagano  and his scheme and every and in the  coaching staff he's brought in the  defensive side and they just been diving  in and we got just a veteran veteran  group on a sunbath side of the ball  they're very savvy - like you so they're  just embracing the grind of what is  offseason OTAs and picking up this new  new defense and I can't wait to go  against them soon in practice we're  gonna get it going and we're just super  talented so when they put their mind to  something and just learn this new scheme  and attack and hopefully they're gonna  be just as dominant as they were last  year last year nobody really expected  anything from the Bears and you guys  overachieved and surprised a lot of  people what's the difference this year  the mindset because there is that burden  there's that expectation that you're  gonna win the division again does it  change the way you think about things  this time of year  a little bit I think all those  expectations that we overachieved were  external we knew what we had in the  locker room and we knew how many games  we could win and we felt like every week  we're in it and then we just we felt  like we should have won more games than  we did last year so all those  expectations that we overachieved where  external last year and the the pressure  that's out from outside forces a while  as well so we're just going to control  control do go one game in as a week and  whether people believes in us they think  we should hit this number of wins or  what they didn't last year so we know  what we're capable of we know what we  have in the locker room we're very  confident group and we're excited for  this year and the the the bar is  definitely set higher so we know that  and it's not from who's setting that  expectation on the outside we're setting  that standard for itself and we're gonna  go chase it and get after it so we're  very pumped all right Mitch hey we  appreciate your time we'll check out the  gone rogue snacks available at  supermarkets and convenience stores  nationwide also at amazon.com for more  information people go to gone rogue  snacks calm all the best Mitch look  forward to talking to you again soon  appreciate thank you yes  get you some gone rogue chips  hi I'm Mike Tirico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from NBC  Sports

